      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Asian Pacific Society of Nephrology.",
        "AbstractText": "We present a case of a foetal sonographic finding of hyper-echogenic kidneys, which led to a strategic series of genetic tests and identified a homozygous mutation (c.424C > T, p. R142*) in the NPHP3 gene. Our study provides a rare presentation of NPHP3-related ciliopathy and adds to the mutation spectrum of the gene, being the first one from Pakistani population. With a thorough literature review, it also advocates for molecular assessment of ciliopathies to improve risk estimate for future pregnancies, and identify predisposed asymptomatic carriers."
      },
